\par 
\par \plain\f2\fs32 Version 5.5\plain\f2\fs24 
\par \plain\f4\fs24 For information regarding what's new for this version, please see the 'What's New' section of the on-line help.
\par \plain\f4\fs20 
\par \pard\plain\f4\fs28\b New Installation Program 
\par \plain\f4\fs24 As of version 5, the installation program will automatically detect and delete any existing version of ReportBuilder installed on your system.  The entire root directory in which ReportBuilder is installed will be deleted.  It is therefore imperative that you backup any custom work  that may reside in this directory before installing this version.  Also, the default install directory is now:
\par 
\par \pard\li720\plain\f4\fs24 $(DELPHI)\\RBuilder
\par \pard\plain\f4\fs24 
\par This directory is used regardless of whether you are installing ReportBuilder Standard, Professional, or Enterprise.
\par \pard\tx360\plain\f2\fs32 
\par 
\par Delphi 5 Release Notes:\plain\f2\fs24\b 
\par \plain\f4\fs28\b 
\par 1. New for Delphi 5
\par \plain\f4\fs24 
\par ReportBuilder contains full support for the InterBase Express (IBX) and ADO components that ship with some versions of Delphi 5. 
\par 
\par When using IBX or ADO components with a ReportBuilder report, simply connect a DBPipeline to a standard Delphi DataSource component.
\par 
\par When using the query tools available within the Data workspace of the Report Designer, configure the Designer component as shown in the end-user database examples provided in \'85RBuilder\\Demos\\EndUser Databases.
\par 
\par \plain\f4\fs28\b 2. Issues with Frames\plain\f2\fs20\b 
\par \plain\f4\fs24 
\par Delphi 5 Frames (TFrame) are containers that enable collections of components to be visually configured and re-used. Unlike form inheritance, however, Delphi 5 does not permit new components to be added to frame descendants (i.e. frames embedded on forms or other frames). 
\par 
\par Therefore, if a Report object is placed on a frame, the report layout must be maintained entirely in the top level ancestor. You cannot access a form containing the frame and add report components, nor can new report layouts be loaded from templates. 
\par 
\par ReportBuilder's DBPipeline and BDEPipeline components cannot currently be used with frames. Both of these components automatically create Field components (i.e. AutoCreateFields) when a dataset is opened. This behavior will cause access violations if a data pipeline is placed in a descendant frame.
\par 
\par \plain\f2\fs32 
\par Installation Notes\plain\f2\fs20\b 
\par \plain\f2\fs20 
\par \plain\f4\fs28\cf0\b 1. Install ReportBuilder\plain\f2\fs20\cf0\b 
\par \plain\f4\fs24\cf0 The installation program will copy files into the ..\\RBuilder directory, add the ReportBuilder components to a 'RBuilder' tab of the Delphi component palette, install the ReportBuilder help into the Delphi help system, and install TeeChart support (if you have TeeChart installed). 
\par 
\par If after installing ReportBuilder and launching Delphi, you do not see the RBuilder tab on the Delphi component palette, access the Component | Install Packages menu option, go to the bottom of the package list, and check each of the ReportBuilder packages.  If the packages are already checked, access the Component | Configure Palette\'85 menu option and move the RBuilder tab up the list, positioning it right before the 'Data Controls' tab.  This will allow you to see the RBuilder tab without scrolling right on the Delphi component palette.
\par \plain\f2\fs24\cf0 
\par \plain\f4\fs28\cf0\b 2. Review the on-line help\plain\f2\fs20\cf0\b 
\par \plain\f4\fs24\cf0 If it appears that ReportBuilder is not installed correctly, use the information in the on-line help to troubleshoot your installation.  The on-line help is located in the RBuilder.hlp file in the RBuilder\\Help directory.  From the table of contents, select 'Installing ReportBuilder'.
\par \plain\f2\fs24\cf0\b  
\par \plain\f4\fs28\cf0\b 3. Convert 3.5x Reports\plain\f2\fs20\cf0\b 
\par \plain\f4\fs24\cf0 ReportBuilder will convert reports that were created with previous versions. Please back-up your existing reports before beginning the conversion process.  Reports converted to the current version will not be useable by previous versions of ReportBuilder.
\par 
\par The first time you open your reports, a conversion routine will run, assigning the values of discontinued properties to their new counterparts.  Simply opening and closing a form (and saying Yes to the Save Changes? dialog) is enough to convert the reports contained therein to the current format.  If you have reports in RTM files, load the RTMs into a report object at Delphi design-time and then save the RTM to file.
\par 
\par Due to the nature of the conversion routine, it will take at least 1-2 seconds for the routine to run when converting reports created with a version previous to ReportBuilder 4.0.  When opening reports within Delphi, you may notice that TppCalc declarations at the top of your form appear momentarily and then disappear.  This is normal.  The TppCalc component was discontinued as of version 4.0 and has been replaced by the TppVariable and TppSystemVariable components respectively.
\par 
\par 
\par \plain\f2\fs32\cf0 Version 5.5 - 10/21/2000\plain\f2\fs24\cf0\b 
\par \plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \plain\f4\fs28\cf0\b Fixes
\par \plain\f2\fs24\cf0\b 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 1.\tab JITPipeline did not function properly when main report was being used as a 'driver' for section style subreports.
\par \pard\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 2.\tab Monochrome bitmaps were rendered directly to the printer canvas, even when Image.DirectDraw was false.
\par \pard\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 3.\tab Crosstab based on detail data did not clear properly when no detail records were present.
\par \pard\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 4.\tab The first report saved into an empty rbItem table using the Report Explorer caused an invalid variant error.
\par 
\par 5.\tab Accessing ReportBuilder's help file from within the Report Designer sometimes resulted in a conflict with the Delphi help system.
\par \pard\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 6.\tab In DADE, importing a DataModule raised an error.
\par \pard\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 7.\tab In RAP, property references on access specifiers did not execute property.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\tx360\plain\f2\fs24\cf0\b 
\par \pard\li270\fi-270\plain\f4\fs28\cf0\b Enhancements for 5.5\plain\f2\fs20\cf0 \tab 
\par 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 1.\tab The Second Edition of the Developer's Guide is now available!  See the new PDF file located in the RBuilder\\Developer's Guide directory.
\par 
\par 2.\tab In DADE, DataViews created via the Query Wizard or Query Designer can be visually linked in the Data workspace.
\par 
\par 3.\tab In DADE, the Query Designer and Query Wizard now allow fields to be used in search criteria; search criteria values can now contain function calls or field names.
\par \pard\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 4.\tab KeepTogether.  Memo, RichText, Region and SubReport (child-type) components now provide a KeepTogether property.
\par \pard\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 5.\tab DetailBand.ColumnTraversal. The detail band can now traverse the columns of the report either vertically or horizontally.  Horizontal traversal does not support groups.
\par \pard\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 6.\tab TextAlignment.  The Memo and DBMemo components now support justified text.
\par \pard\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 7.\tab The DetailBand.DataPipeline property has been deprecated.  Reports using this property will function properly, but new reports should be configured using SubReports for all detail datasets.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 8.\tab DataPipeline components no longer participate in the report engine caching scheme.  This enhancement allows a single data pipeline to be used for multiple reports.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li270\fi-270\plain\f4\fs28\cf0\b 
\par Recent Enhancements\plain\f2\fs20\cf0 
\par 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 1.\tab RAP.  Report Application Pascal debuts in ReportBuilder Enterprise.  Be the envy of your friends and relatives - code Object Pascal at run-time. For comprehensive information about RAP, see the RAP Reference in the on-line help.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 2.\tab The Report Explorer now has FolderOptions, ItemOptions, and an ItemAction property, which allow you to control the capabilities of the Explorer. For example, you can configure these properties such that the user can print reports, but cannot create new reports or folders. Or you can change the double-click behavior such that the Print Preview form is displayed instead of the Report Designer.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 3.\tab The AutoSearch Dialog now provides a 'Show All Values' feature, which allows the user to easily disable search criteria that they do not need.  The feature is essentially the opposite of Mandatory, and is not available for search criteria where Mandatory is True.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 4.\tab LookAhead totals.  You can now display totals that would normally appear in the group footer, footer or summary bands in the group header, header and title bands.  Simply configure a Variable or DBCalc as you normally would, place it in the header band, and set the LookAhead property to True. 
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 5.\tab Label Wizard. A new Label Template Wizard has been added to the Report Designer. You can select from over 300 pre-defined label templates with the Label Template Wizard. 
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs28\cf0\b 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 6.\tab Simplified JITPipeline. We added new public properties RecordCount, RecordIndex, and InitialIndex to enable the JITPipeline to automatically track record indexing. In addition, using Master/Detail JITPipelines no longer requires the user to code event-handlers related to data linkage. Please see the main report demo application for examples.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 7.\tab The PrinterSetup.Copies setting is now handled internally by ReportBuilder rather than relying on the printer driver.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 8.\tab Crosstab Styles. We added new Style property to Crosstab. Current options are Standard and Repeated Captions. When the Repeated Captions style is selected, the appropriate row or column captions are repeatable on all relevant pages.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 9.\tab Crosstab Events. We added new 'GetText' events to the Crosstab component to enable more customization of output. See ct0128.pas of the Demos\\Crosstab project for an example of using these new events: OnGetCaptionText, OnGetTotalCaptionText, OnGetValueText, and OnGetTotalValueText.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 10.\tab AutoJoin.  We added 'disabled tables' to the Query Wizard and Query Designer when AutoJoin is being used. When a table is selected for a query, the 'available tables list' automatically disables tables that have no pre-defined relationship with the selected table(s).
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 11.\tab AutoSearch - The new AutoSearch dialog allows you to display search criteria values in a 'Query-by-Form' format before printing a report. You can assign the search criteria values entered by the user to standard Delphi data access components. The end-user can visually define AutoSearch criteria in the Query Designer.  For examples of this new feature, see the ...RBuilder Pro 4\\Demos\\AutoSearch directory.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 12.\tab The new DataDictionary Builder can be accessed by double-clicking on the Data Dictionary component.  This utility allows you to quickly and easily generate and maintain the entries in your data dictionary tables.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 13.\tab The Data Dictionary now contains a new feature called AutoJoin. AutoJoin allows you to specify the valid relationships between the tables of your database.  These relationships are then used to automatically build joins when end-users select more than one table in the Query Wizard or Query Designer.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 14.\tab New database-specific end-user examples have been developed for Access 97, Advantage, InterBase, Oracle 8, SQL Server 7, Sybase ASE 11, Sybase ASA 6, SQL Anywhere 5.  You can find these examples in the \'85RBuilder Pro 4\\Demos\\EndUser Databases directory.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 15.\tab TeeChart support  has been enhanced.  Based on the version of TeeChart that you have installed in Delphi, the ReportBuilder installation program will install support for either the Tee50 package (for the TeeChart delivered with Delphi) or the new Tee45 package (for TeeChart Pro 4.03 for Delphi 5 from TeeMach).
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 16.\tab The Print Dialog has been updated to the Office97 'look-and-feel'.  Also, a new capability that allows the printing of odd or even pages has been added.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 17.\tab International language support has been updated.  The translation application (rbStringTranslator) has been redesigned and the resource files (rbPrint.rc, rbIDE.rc and rbDADE.rc) have been updated to contain all of the strings in the user-interface. In order to create your own custom translation, download the new application from: http://www.digital-metaphors.com/lang/rbLang.exe
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 18.\tab A new public property called EnableProcessMessages has been added to the Report and ArchiveReader components. This property controls whether or not ReportBuilder will make calls to Application.ProcessMessages when generating report pages.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 21.\tab The TSpinButton control has been replaced with the TUpDown control throughout the ReportBuilder user-interface.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 22.\tab A new set of options has been introduced on the File menu for opening and saving subreports. When you are working within a subreport layout (i.e. you have clicked a subreport tab), the Open and Save menu options will now refer to the entire report (i.e. main) instead of the subreport. This means that selecting Save from within a subreport will save the entire report.  The new menu options 'Load SubReport' and 'Save SubReport' refer only to the currently active subreport and replace the previous behavior of the Open and Save menu options.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 23.\tab The Print Preview form now displays the message Page 'X' until the last page of the report has been previewed.  Once the last page of the report has been previewed (or if the report has been set to psTwoPass), the message will display in the format Page 'X' of 'X'.
\par \pard\li360\fi-360\tx360\plain\f4\fs28\cf0 
\par \pard\li720\fi-360\tx360\tx720\plain\f4\fs24\cf0 24.\tab The Report Explorer now uses RBuilder.ini, rather than RExplore.ini, to save the state of the form.\plain\f2\fs20\cf0 
\par }
␀